WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.240
Adult rodents make new neurons.

2
00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.020
Which cell makes them, and how many are kept?

3
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.480
They appear in two places.

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.340
One is the subventricular zone, in the wall of the lateral ventricles.

5
00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.440
Its young neurons migrate forward in chains to the olfactory bulb.

6
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.200
The other is the dentate gyrus of the hippocampus.

7
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:27.020
There, the rate falls steeply with age.

8
00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:31.573
Four kinds of cell sit in that wall.

9
00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:35.573
Ependymal cells line it, with astrocyte-like B cells beneath.

10
00:00:36.617 --> 00:00:37.977
Both divide rarely.

11
00:00:38.957 --> 00:00:43.637
Fast-dividing C cells multiply, and young neurons, the A cells, migrate away.

12
00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:50.087
In 1999, Fiona Doetsch and colleagues infused adult mice with a drug that kills

13
00:00:50.087 --> 00:00:52.547
cells copying DNA, then stopped.

14
00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:54.770
Pause and predict.

15
00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:56.610
Which cells survive?

16
00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:58.910
And which one rebuilds the zone?

17
00:01:05.283 --> 00:01:07.863
The fast dividers and most neuroblasts died.

18
00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:10.003
The rare dividers survived.

19
00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:13.127
Then the astrocyte-like cells divided.

20
00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:17.267
Precursors came back, then neuroblasts, in the normal order.

21
00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.350
That makes them the leading candidate, not yet proof.

22
00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:29.550
Proof needs an inherited label showing the neurons descend from an astrocyte-like

23
00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.590
cell, in the same cells as neuron identity.

24
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:38.963
This retrovirus writes its genes into the chromosome of a dividing cell, so every

25
00:01:38.963 --> 00:01:40.303
descendant inherits them.

26
00:01:41.233 --> 00:01:43.813
This virus enters only through one receptor.

27
00:01:44.713 --> 00:01:48.453
The mice were engineered to make it only in cells making GFAP.

28
00:01:49.533 --> 00:01:53.433
So in untreated mice, only astrocyte-like cells were infected.

29
00:01:54.393 --> 00:01:57.313
Later, the marker turned up in new olfactory bulb neurons.

30
00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:06.667
The dentate gyrus follows the same plan, with radial, astrocyte-like stem cells.

31
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:09.930
How many are kept?

32
00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.610
In mice, many newborn cells die early, mostly within the first days.

33
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:20.390
Later, while they mature, survival also depends partly on their own activity.

34
00:02:21.533 --> 00:02:26.513
Young neurons lacking NMDA receptors survive less well than their neighbours.

35
00:02:27.493 --> 00:02:29.413
Other survival signals may help too.

36
00:02:30.417 --> 00:02:34.077
More new neurons can mean more division, or more young cells kept.

37
00:02:34.917 --> 00:02:36.537
Two time points help tell them apart.

38
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:42.210
After one dose of BrdU, a one-day count is an index of division.

39
00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:48.270
At four weeks, label plus a neuron protein counts labelled cells that are neurons by

40
00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:49.270
then.

41
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:50.683
Pause and predict.

42
00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:55.303
If running acted only on division, what would you see at each time point?

43
00:03:01.717 --> 00:03:06.277
More labelled cells at one day, and more new neurons at four weeks, in the same

44
00:03:06.277 --> 00:03:07.277
proportion.

45
00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:10.990
In those mouse studies, running mainly raised division.

46
00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.730
Enriched housing mainly raised survival.

47
00:03:18.183 --> 00:03:22.483
Takeaway: the stem cell looks glial, and born is not the same as kept.
